.Sh "CONFIG FILES"
All under the single uplift data dir
.Pa ~/.omlx/uplift/
(overridable with
.Ev UPLIFT_HOME ;
.Ic OMLX_BASE_PATH
does
.Em not
move it, so the vanilla and omlx-dev servers share one patch store):
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa metrics.sqlite3
UPLIFT'S OWN metrics database.
The collector writes sub-hour-resolution time series and per-request rows
here.
Vanilla omlx's
.Pa ~/.omlx/usage.sqlite3
(hourly rollups) is opened strictly READ-ONLY and never written by Uplift.
.It Pa env_overrides.json
Uplift-stored experimental
.Dv OMLX_*
tunables (the allow-list shown in Settings).
Seeded into the process environment at interpreter startup by the autopatch
hook.
A genuine launch-time environment variable (launchd plist, shell, CLI)
ALWAYS wins; stored values fill only the gaps.
Effect class per knob is shown in the UI: immediate / restart model /
restart server.
.It Pa patches.json
Patch manifest: declarative desired state for every patch carrier
(state machine: pending -> applied -> update_available / needs_review /
failed / disabled / obsolete).
Stored diffs, backups and this manifest live entirely uplift-side.
.It Pa patches/
Stored diff files and byte-exact pre-apply backups.
.It Pa patches.lock
Reconcile lock (startup and CLI share it).
.It Pa patches.disabled
Kill-switch sentinel: when present, startup only verifies patches and
boots omlx unpatched.
.Ic omlx-uplift
patches disable-all
creates it; delete the file (or re-enable patches in the UI) to resume.
.It Pa kernel-backups/
Byte-exact originals behind
.Ic kernel
rebuild .
.It Pa dev.json
.Em omlx-dev
config: origin, sync_ref, formula branch, port, base path, share map,
built_sha.
Server truth by design — the only server-backed piece of the settings
surface; the dashboard reads and writes it through
.Pa /uplift/api/dev/* .
.It Pa dev-src/
The omlx checkout that build patches materialize in
(Em uplift-dev
branch;
.Ic brew
clones from here).
.El
.Pp
Browser-side settings (theme, layout, locale) are client-side only: they
live in localStorage, never in these files.
.Sh PATCHES
You upload unified diffs; Uplift applies them to the live omlx package tree
with a strict applier and keeps byte-exact backups for restore.
.Pp
At every server start, BEFORE omlx.server is imported, the .pth hook runs
a reconcile: applied+unchanged patches are skipped (fast verify), enabled
patches whose target still matches are (re)applied in order, failures turn
into needs_review (WARNING badge) and boot continues UNPATCHED for that
one patch only.
If any file changed on disk, the process re-execs itself ONCE before
engines start, so patched code is served right away.
.Pp
Hard limits: the whole reconcile is time-boxed to 60 s (the rest defers to
the next start), at most one re-exec per boot, and every error path boots
omlx unpatched — a broken patch can never prevent the server from
starting.
.Pp
Guard rails: diffs touching compiled kernel sources
.Po omlx/custom_kernels/ Pc
or resolving outside the keg are HELD until you approve per reason code;
.Ic omlx-uplift
kernel rebuild
handles the compiled-artifact side.
.Sh "DEV PATCHES AND OMLX-DEV"
Patch scopes (manifest
.Va scope :
omlx ,
dev
or
.Ic both ) :
omlx applies the pruned overlay to the vanilla keg only;
dev materializes the full diff (tests included) on the
.Em uplift-dev
branch and never touches a keg;
.Ic both
does both (the keg gets the pruned overlay).
Legacy
.Dq runtime Ns / Ns No build
values normalize to omlx/dev.
Dev-scope patches never touch a vanilla keg.
Uplift stacks them as one commit per patch on the
.Em uplift-dev
branch of the
.Pa dev-src
checkout, then rebuilds the separate
.Em omlx-dev
formula from that tip.
Rebuild required after every change
( Ic dev
install ,
the dashboard's
.Dq Rebuild omlx-dev
/
.Dq Rebuild & restart
buttons, or
.Pa POST /uplift/api/dev/build ) ;
after a successful build the dashboard shows
.Dv RESTART NEEDED
until the service reloads the new keg
( Ic dev
restart endpoint or
.Ic brew
services restart omlx-dev ) .
Enabled build patches are re-gated against every new base BEFORE the
reinstall; failures are marked needs_review and listed in the build
result, never silently skipped.
.Pp
omlx-dev coexists with vanilla: separate port (default 8001, via
.Dv OMLX_PORT ) ,
separate data root (default
.Pa ~/.omlx-dev ,
via
.Dv OMLX_BASE_PATH ) ,
separate service.
Shareable knobs (models directory, model settings, model profiles) are a
per-knob symlink decision; refusing to hide real dev-side data behind a
symlink is deliberate.
Works only after
.Em omlx-dev
has been set up
( Ic dev
bootstrap ) .
.Sh "OMLX UPGRADE WORKFLOW"
A vanilla upgrade replaces the keg and silently unmounts Uplift (the .pth
dies with the old keg).
Until you re-mount, omlx serves VANILLA.
Sequence:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
brew upgrade omlx
omlx-uplift install          # BEFORE the restart, or first boot is vanilla
launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/sh.brew.omlx
.Ed
.Pp
At that first patched boot every enabled omlx-scope patch is re-applied
against the NEW keg: diffs whose context still matches apply
automatically; diffs broken by upstream drift go to needs_review and need
a re-based upload in the UI (Settings -> Patches, or
.Ic omlx-uplift
patches status ) .
.Pp
Your data survives untouched:
.Pa ~/.omlx/uplift/
is outside the keg.
.Ic brew
upgrade omlx-uplift
needs no remount: the .pth points at the stable
.Pa opt/
symlink.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
When set, CLI output is uncoloured (also: non-tty stdout).
.It Ev OMLX_BASE_PATH
Relocates the omlx data directory (models, usage database, and the omlx-dev
data root).
The uplift patch store is deliberately NOT relocated by it — see
.Ev UPLIFT_HOME .
.It Ev UPLIFT_HOME
Relocates the single uplift data dir (default
.Pa ~/.omlx/uplift ) .
.It Ev OMLX_PORT / OMLX_DEV_PORT
Server ports (omlx-dev defaults to 8001 via its launchd environment).
.El
.Sh "EXIT STATUS"
Exit status 0 means success; 1 means a usage error, a failed
mount check, or a refused/failed operation.
